<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Keys Xcode cannot generate from INFOPLIST_KEY_* build settings. Merged with the generated Info.plist.

  App Transport Security trade-off
  ================================
  Lumen talks to servers the *user* types in: LAN IPs (http://192.168.1.50:11434), mDNS names
  (http://mac-studio.local:11434), VPN / tailnet hostnames (http://box.tail1234.ts.net:11434), and
  public HTTPS endpoints. Many self-hosted LLM servers only speak plain HTTP.

  * NSAllowsLocalNetworking alone only exempts unqualified names, .local names and IP literals,
    so a VPN hostname over http:// would be blocked.
  * Apple IGNORES NSAllowsArbitraryLoads whenever NSAllowsLocalNetworking (or the web-content /
    media variants) is also present, so the two cannot be combined to mean "local + anything".

  We therefore set NSAllowsArbitraryLoads alone. Cost: ATS no longer forces TLS for any host, so
  the app itself must make the risk visible — every http:// server shows a "Not encrypted" badge,
  and the app never sends traffic to hosts the user did not configure. HTTPS servers still get
  full certificate validation by URLSession. App Review justification: "connects to
  user-configured, self-hosted servers that commonly do not offer TLS".
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSAppTransportSecurity</key>
	<dict>
		<key>NSAllowsArbitraryLoads</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>
	<key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Lumen connects to AI model servers on your local network, such as Ollama or LM Studio running on another computer.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
